source_env .envrc.sops

use sops_if_exists .env.secrets.postgres.sops-encrypted
use sops_if_exists .env.secrets.snowflake.user.sops-encrypted

# A multi-line value (the keypair's PEM) goes on one line, double-quoted, each
# newline written as \n: sops refuses a real newline in dotenv
# (https://github.com/getsops/sops/issues/965) and keeps the quoted line as it
# is; direnv's dotenv parser turns the \n back into newlines. The quotes stay
# in the stored value, so `sops --extract` hands them through
# (https://github.com/getsops/sops/issues/1127), and `sops exec-env` cannot
# read a dotenv bundle under this name at all: read this bundle through
# use_sops only. Any other value goes in single quotes, which direnv takes
# literally: unquoted, a space breaks the whole bundle, and double quotes
# expand `$`. sops reads every \n as a newline and writes it back as \n
# (https://github.com/getsops/sops/issues/1435), so a literal backslash-n
# reaches use_sops intact and any other sops reader as a newline.
use sops_if_exists .env.secrets.snowflake.keypair.sops-encrypted
